From 805947285c48a692768aecb992db043f72db7837 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Fiorillo <nicfio@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:46:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2-subdev: Use the video device's v4l2_dev in open()

Unbinding a sensor driver while something opens its /dev/v4l-subdevN node
oopses the kernel:

  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000008
  RIP: 0010:subdev_open+0x8a/0x190 [videodev]
  Call Trace:
   v4l2_open+0xa9/0x100 [videodev]
   chrdev_open+0xb2/0x230
   do_dentry_open+0x14c/0x440
   vfs_open+0x2e/0xe0
   path_openat+0x82e/0x12d0
   do_filp_open+0xc4/0x170
   do_sys_openat2+0xae/0xe0
   __x64_sys_openat+0x55/0xa0

v4l2_device_unregister_subdev() clears sd->v4l2_dev, then unregisters the
media entity, which clears sd->entity.graph_obj.mdev, and only then
unregisters the device node. subdev_open() dereferences both pointers.
v4l2_open() has checked that the node is registered, but it drops
videodev_lock before calling fops->open(), so the whole unregistration can
run in between: moving video_unregister_device() earlier, or checking the
two pointers in subdev_open(), would only narrow the window.

Neither pointer is needed there. Both are registration state of the
sub-device, cleared on purpose when it goes away, while open() runs on
behalf of the device node. The node has its own pointer to the same
v4l2_device, vdev->v4l2_dev, which is set when the node is registered,
is never cleared, and is backed by the reference __video_register_device()
takes on the v4l2_device and v4l2_device_release() drops. The sub-device's
entity is registered with vdev->v4l2_dev->mdev, so that is the media
device to take the module reference from.

Use them, and there is nothing left in subdev_open() for the
unregistration to change under it. This does not address the lifetime of
the sub-device itself or of the media device when their drivers go away
with file handles open, which is a separate, known limitation.

Reproduced on a CHUWI Hi10 X1 (Alder Lake-N, IPU6) running 6.12.86, at
cycle 7 of a loop unbinding and rebinding a sensor while four processes
opened every /dev/v4l-subdev*. syzbot has since hit the second
dereference on the same line with vimc.

Fixes: 61f5db549dde ("[media] v4l: Make v4l2_subdev inherit from media_entity")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Nicola Fiorillo <nicfio@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-subdev.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-subdev.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-subdev.c
index a07d77e58..65e1568b1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-subdev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-subdev.c
@@ -96,6 +96,7 @@ static int subdev_open(struct file *file)
 {
 	struct video_device *vdev = video_devdata(file);
 	struct v4l2_subdev *sd = vdev_to_v4l2_subdev(vdev);
+	struct media_device *mdev = vdev->v4l2_dev->mdev;
 	struct v4l2_subdev_fh *subdev_fh;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -112,10 +113,10 @@ static int subdev_open(struct file *file)
 	v4l2_fh_init(&subdev_fh->vfh, vdev);
 	v4l2_fh_add(&subdev_fh->vfh, file);
 
-	if (sd->v4l2_dev->mdev && sd->entity.graph_obj.mdev->dev) {
+	if (mdev && mdev->dev) {
 		struct module *owner;
 
-		owner = sd->entity.graph_obj.mdev->dev->driver->owner;
+		owner = mdev->dev->driver->owner;
 		if (!try_module_get(owner)) {
 			ret = -EBUSY;
 			goto err;

base-commit: 2dcdfb625c3b8fe87454e19dfbc54b3e3f0ad70e
